From: prplmesh OpenWrt package
Subject: [PATCH] controller: roaming threshold from the mesh links

Derive the STA RCPI reporting threshold of the Metric Reporting Policy
per agent and radio from the mesh itself: the RSSI at which the agent
hears its nearest mesh neighbour (wireless backhaul link) plus 4 dB,
adjusted by roaming_band_pathloss_delta_db when the radio and the link
are on different bands, clamped to -80..-55 dBm. A client below it is
about as far away as the other agent and is logged as a roaming
candidate, whether the RCPI came from an agent-initiated report or from
the periodic AP metrics. The threshold is recomputed every 15 seconds
and the policy resent when it moves by 3 dB or more. The configured
sta_reporting_rcpi_threshold is only used when there is no wireless mesh
link to derive it from.

